The user presented a `NetCDFGeographicMap` class for loading NetCDF files but faced issues when implementing it. They sought guidance on adjusting the class to automatically extract latitude and longitude data from NetCDF files instead of passing it as parameters. Additionally, they requested a feature to transform longitudes from the range of 0-360 to -180 to 180. 

In response, I recommended creating helper functions, `rangeFromCenters` and `wrappedLongitude`, and modifying the `loadNetCDF` method to correctly identify dimension names and indices. When the user encountered an error regarding evenly spaced coordinates, I explained that the tolerance for checking spacing should account for floating-point precision limitations. A revised method with an appropriate tolerance was suggested to resolve the issue.
